1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:02,800
Two divers surfaced at the Great Barrier Reef.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,000
Their boat was gone.

3
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:06,230
January 1998.

4
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,880
St Crispin's Reef, off Port Douglas.

5
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:12,910
Tom and Eileen Lonergan, experienced American divers.

6
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:16,660
Before leaving, the Outer Edge crew reportedly counted heads.

7
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:19,960
By one account, two other divers were counted twice.

8
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:22,120
On paper, everyone was aboard.

9
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,540
The boat headed home.

10
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,620
Nobody noticed they were missing.

11
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:29,240
Two days later, the crew found their bag still aboard.

12
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:30,060
Inside:

13
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,720
their wallets and passports.

14
00:00:32,090 --> 00:00:33,970
Only then did the search begin.

15
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:35,770
Searchers found their gear.

16
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:36,600
Not them.

17
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:39,520
A buoyancy vest washed ashore up the coast.

18
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:40,710
Then a wetsuit.

19
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:44,600
Months later, a dive slate, reportedly asking for rescue.

20
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:47,040
Tom and Eileen were never found.

21
00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:49,660
What happened in the water is unknown.

22
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:51,670
The skipper was acquitted.

23
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:53,810
The company was fined and closed.

24
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:55,820
Queensland tightened its rules.

25
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:59,100
Divers must now be counted twice, independently.

26
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:01,680
Because one wrong count is all it takes...
